WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.582
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online Advanced.

2
00:00:05.882 --> 00:00:09.013
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.313 --> 00:00:16.447
Unit eleven: Education Reform. In this unit, you will discuss how education systems should change.

4
00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.428
pedagogy.

5
00:00:19.128 --> 00:00:22.521
pedagogy means the method and practice of teaching.

6
00:00:22.821 --> 00:00:25.970
Modern pedagogy focuses on active learning.

7
00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:29.984
Your turn. Say: pedagogy.

8
00:00:32.684 --> 00:00:33.754
pedagogy.

9
00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:36.424
standardised testing.

10
00:00:37.124 --> 00:00:42.003
standardised testing means the same exam given to all students to compare results.

11
00:00:42.303 --> 00:00:45.464
Critics say standardised testing narrows the curriculum.

12
00:00:46.164 --> 00:00:49.942
Your turn. Say: standardised testing.

13
00:00:52.642 --> 00:00:54.282
standardised testing.

14
00:00:55.283 --> 00:00:56.935
holistic education.

15
00:00:57.635 --> 00:01:03.744
holistic education means education that develops the whole person, not only academic skills.

16
00:01:04.044 --> 00:01:07.773
Holistic education includes arts, sport and character.

17
00:01:08.473 --> 00:01:12.159
Your turn. Say: holistic education.

18
00:01:14.859 --> 00:01:16.348
holistic education.

19
00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:18.746
curriculum reform.

20
00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:22.990
curriculum reform means changes to what is taught in schools.

21
00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:26.369
The curriculum reform introduced coding lessons.

22
00:01:27.069 --> 00:01:30.650
Your turn. Say: curriculum reform.

23
00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:34.664
curriculum reform.

24
00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:37.719
inquiry-based learning.

25
00:01:38.419 --> 00:01:43.484
inquiry-based learning means learning by asking questions and investigating.

26
00:01:43.784 --> 00:01:46.840
Inquiry-based learning makes students more curious.

27
00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:51.864
Your turn. Say: inquiry-based learning.

28
00:01:54.564 --> 00:01:56.238
inquiry-based learning.

29
00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.599
rote memorisation.

30
00:01:59.299 --> 00:02:04.074
rote memorisation means learning by repeating information without understanding.

31
00:02:04.374 --> 00:02:08.010
Rote memorisation helps in exams but not in life.

32
00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:11.943
Your turn. Say: rote memorisation.

33
00:02:14.643 --> 00:02:15.969
rote memorisation.

34
00:02:16.983 --> 00:02:18.669
educational equity.

35
00:02:19.369 --> 00:02:24.573
educational equity means fair access to quality education for all students.

36
00:02:24.873 --> 00:02:28.324
Educational equity requires support for rural schools.

37
00:02:29.024 --> 00:02:32.570
Your turn. Say: educational equity.

38
00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:36.840
educational equity.

39
00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:39.025
teacher training.

40
00:02:39.725 --> 00:02:43.768
teacher training means programmes that prepare and develop teachers.

41
00:02:44.068 --> 00:02:47.217
Better teacher training improves learning outcomes.

42
00:02:47.917 --> 00:02:51.173
Your turn. Say: teacher training.

43
00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:55.048
teacher training.

44
00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:58.224
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:58.524 --> 00:03:03.704
Rithy, if you could change one thing about education in Cambodia, what would it be?

46
00:03:05.017 --> 00:03:09.817
The reliance on rote memorisation. The introduction of inquiry-based learning would help.

47
00:03:11.117 --> 00:03:15.136
But standardised testing still rewards memorisation, doesn't it?

48
00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:21.088
Exactly. Any curriculum reform needs a change in assessment too.

49
00:03:22.383 --> 00:03:24.487
What about educational equity?

50
00:03:25.783 --> 00:03:30.607
The improvement of rural schools should be a priority. The gap is enormous.

51
00:03:31.917 --> 00:03:33.220
And teacher training?

52
00:03:34.517 --> 00:03:39.259
Absolutely. The success of any reform depends on the quality of teachers.

53
00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:43.037
Grammar focus: Nominalisation.

54
00:03:43.337 --> 00:03:47.125
Nominalisation means turning verbs or adjectives into nouns.

55
00:03:47.425 --> 00:03:52.060
Introduce becomes the introduction of; improve becomes the improvement of.

56
00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:55.578
It makes academic writing more formal and concise.

57
00:03:55.878 --> 00:04:01.814
Nominalisation makes writing more formal and lets you pack more information into the subject.

58
00:04:02.817 --> 00:04:06.375
Now read and listen. Learning for the Real World.

59
00:04:06.675 --> 00:04:11.008
Across Asia, education systems are under pressure to change.

60
00:04:12.317 --> 00:04:17.706
For decades, success was measured mainly through standardised testing and rote memorisation.

61
00:04:19.017 --> 00:04:25.405
However, employers increasingly demand creativity, communication and problem-solving.

62
00:04:26.717 --> 00:04:34.301
The introduction of inquiry-based learning encourages students to ask questions rather than repeat answers.

63
00:04:35.617 --> 00:04:42.272
Holistic education also places greater emphasis on wellbeing, arts and character.

64
00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:49.379
Yet the implementation of reforms is often slow, especially in rural areas.

65
00:04:50.683 --> 00:04:56.514
Educational equity requires investment in teacher training and school resources.

66
00:04:57.817 --> 00:05:03.949
Ultimately, the transformation of education depends on teachers more than on policies.

67
00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:08.018
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

68
00:05:08.318 --> 00:05:10.980
The method and practice of teaching is blank.

69
00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:16.559
A, pedagogy. B, curriculum reform. C, rote memorisation.

70
00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:23.327
The answer is A: pedagogy.

71
00:05:24.817 --> 00:05:26.839
The noun form of 'improve' is blank.

72
00:05:27.139 --> 00:05:31.780
A, improving. B, improvement. C, improver.

73
00:05:35.783 --> 00:05:38.178
The answer is B: improvement.

74
00:05:39.683 --> 00:05:43.529
'They developed the city quickly' → 'The rapid blank of the city...'

75
00:05:43.829 --> 00:05:48.167
A, develop. B, development. C, developed.

76
00:05:52.183 --> 00:05:54.287
The answer is B: development.

77
00:05:55.783 --> 00:05:59.048
Fair access to quality education for all is blank.

78
00:05:59.348 --> 00:06:04.952
A, educational equity. B, standardised testing. C, teacher training.

79
00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:12.076
The answer is A: educational equity.

80
00:06:13.583 --> 00:06:17.557
According to the text, employers increasingly demand blank.

81
00:06:17.857 --> 00:06:24.877
A, memorisation. B, creativity and problem-solving. C, exam scores.

82
00:06:28.883 --> 00:06:32.415
The answer is B: creativity and problem-solving.

83
00:06:33.917 --> 00:06:39.344
Now it's your turn. Part one: What is the most important reform for schools in Cambodia?

84
00:06:44.644 --> 00:06:50.800
Part two: Use nominalisation to present your proposal, two benefits and one challenge.

85
00:06:57.100 --> 00:07:08.683
In my opinion, the introduction of inquiry-based learning is essential. Its benefits include greater curiosity and stronger problem-solving. The main challenge is the training of enough teachers.

86
00:07:08.983 --> 00:07:10.727
That is a well-argued answer!

87
00:07:11.717 --> 00:07:16.145
Great work today! You learned eight new words and nominalisation.

88
00:07:16.445 --> 00:07:19.992
Today's value is pride in learning. Be proud of what you learned.

89
00:07:20.292 --> 00:07:22.967
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

90
00:07:23.267 --> 00:07:26.070
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

